refs: 
https://docs.micropython.org/en/latest/reference/mp.html#mp-command-fs
https://docs.micropython.org/en/latest/reference/packages.html#packages

Note: mpremote ... will do all of the following but have alias mp=mpremote

mp repl                 # Connect to REPL

mp ls                   # List files on device

mp cp adc.py :adc.py    # Copy one file from host dir to device main dir

mp cp -r common :common # Copy a directory from local host to device

mp cp -r :common common # Copy a directory from device to local  Note the ":" means device 

mp run test_adc.py      # Run a python script

mp soft-reset           # Soft reset

mp fs cp main.py :main.py # copies main.py from the current local directory to the remote filesystem

mp rm -r -v  :libs      # will remove the libs directory and all its child items from the device. -v show files being removed.
 
mp fs cat X.py          # shows the contents of X.py

mp mip install gitlab:org/repo@branch    #installs module/package from github 

mp mip install --target /flash/third-party functools   # Install the functools package from micropython-lib to the /flash/third-party directory on the device. See Package management.

print(open("boot.py").read())       # to see file contents while in mp repl
